<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="088" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>UAT-1/5/6/7: the Save tab keeps its form after a save (Saved state, Open Document, View Document opens the Spaarke record in the Spaarke app) and the name-collision prompt offers Open</title>
    <phase>6 UAT round 3 (2026-10-03)</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies production `.ts`/`.tsx` (`SaveFlow.tsx`, `useSaveFlow.ts`, `openRecordLauncher.ts`) and BFF `.cs` (`OfficeService.cs` collision refusal, `OfficeEndpoints.cs` redaction), plus tests on both sides.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The collision change widens what a 409 carries (the existing document's id) — an information-disclosure judgment that must stay behind the existing Read gate; and the post-save state machine touches the save spine (version vs create).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>UAT3-W1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Wave W1 with 092 (client-only Find). Disjoint files: 088 owns `SaveFlow.tsx`, `useSaveFlow.ts`, `errorMessages.ts`, `DocumentProfileSection.tsx`, `openRecordLauncher.ts`, the build setting, and the BFF collision code; it MUST NOT edit `App.tsx`, `FindView.tsx`, `FindResultsList.tsx` (092's). 088 is the only W1 task that runs `dotnet`.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>frontend, office-addins, typescript, bff-api, save-flow, unit-test, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1.5 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Owner UAT round 3 (2026-10-03), items UAT-1, UAT-5, UAT-6 and UAT-7, plus the owner's answers the same day: "Keep the form" after a save, and record links must open in the Spaarke app. Record: `notes/042-uat-round3-2026-10-03.md` §1, §2, §3a.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer on the Office add-in: React 19 + Fluent UI v9 task pane, Office.js, and the BFF Office save path.</role>

  <goal>After a save, the Save tab stays on the form: a confirmation bar at the top (View Document opens the Spaarke record in the Spaarke app; Copy Link), the profile below, and a footer with Open Document to the left of a gray "Saved" button that becomes "Save version" when the name changes or the profile is re-generated. A name collision offers Open when the user can read the other document.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      - **Design chosen by the owner (2026-10-03, "Keep the form")**:
        ```
        [✔ Saved to Spaarke · {record}   [View Document] [Copy Link]]
        Document name [..........]
        Profile  (type, TL;DR, summary, keywords)  [Generate Profile]
        [Cancel]                    [Open Document] [Saved (gray, disabled)]
        name edited / profile re-generated  →  [Open Document] [Save version]
        ```
      - **Today**: a successful save replaces the whole form with `renderSuccessState` (`SaveFlow.tsx:1151-1182`);
        "View Document" (1171-1173, `handleViewDocument` 1077-1081) opens `savedDocumentUrl`, the stored file's
        Graph `webUrl` (Word for the web; server `OfficeService.cs:1044`, `:1705`, `DocumentResult` 1193-1203).
        `App.tsx` passes no `onViewDocument`, so `SaveView.tsx:235-245` does `window.open`. The hook already exposes
        `savedDocumentId` (`useSaveFlow.ts:297/488/654/793`).
      - **Open document record** today: `SaveFlow.tsx:754-764` (handler), 1437-1447 (a subtle button inside the
        Profile section), shown when `openRecordAvailable` (739: `canOpenRecord &amp;&amp; process.env.ORG_URL`) and a
        resolved document id. It calls `openRecord` (`services/openRecordLauncher.ts:125-142`) →
        `buildOpenRecordUrl` (90-92): `${ORG_URL}/main.aspx?etn=…&amp;id=…&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;navbar=off`.
      - **Which app (owner question, answered in `042-uat-round3` §3a)**: the URL names no app, so a record opens in
        the user's DEFAULT model-driven app. The Spaarke user app is **Matter Management**, unique name
        `sprk_MatterManagement` (dev, read live). Name it with `appname=&lt;unique name&gt;` — stable across environments,
        unlike the app GUID — from a new build setting `SPAARKE_APP_NAME` (default `sprk_MatterManagement`) injected
        exactly like `ORG_URL`: `.github/workflows/deploy-office-addins.yml:72` and `webpack.config.js:361`.
        `buildOpenRecordUrl` is also used by `sendEmailService.ts:144`; that consumer gets the app name too.
      - **Save button**: `SaveFlow.tsx:1477-1486` (footer style 214-220, space-between: Cancel left, Save right).
        `isValid` is always true (`useSaveFlow.ts:521`). Reuse CreateTodoView's existing gray "Saved" style
        (`CreateTodoView.tsx:200-204`, `514-518`) — copy it, do not import across views if that couples them.
      - **Profile re-run signal**: `DocumentProfileSection.tsx:173-183` (Generate Profile) has props `documentId` and
        `refreshSignal` only (104-118) — add a callback (e.g. `onProfileGenerated`).
      - **"Save version" after a save**: once saved, the open document IS that Spaarke document, so the next save is a
        version of `savedDocumentId` (FR-11 path, `existingDocumentId` + `isNewVersion`, task 023/024) — reuse the
        existing version-save mode, do not build a second one.
      - **Collision (UAT-5)**: banner `renderCollisionState` `SaveFlow.tsx:1251-1292`; client fields
        `collisionFileName` / `collisionExistingDocumentId` / `collisionExistingDocumentName` (`errorMessages.ts:75-88`,
        386-401). The server sends the existing document's id and name **only if** (a) it is filed to the record this
        save targets (`OfficeService.cs:1469-1494`) **and** (b) the caller can Read it (redaction
        `OfficeEndpoints.cs:552-597`; payload 657-673). The client uses the id's PRESENCE to decide whether to offer
        "Save as new version" (`SaveFlow.tsx:1273`, `1282`). The owner saw only Keep both + Dismiss because (a) failed.
      - **Open the other file**: `GET /api/documents/{id}/open-links` (`FileAccessEndpoints.cs:106-115`, handler
        623-743) — requires Read — returns `DesktopUrl` (`ms-word:https://…`, `DesktopUrlBuilder.FromMime`) and
        `WebUrl`. No add-in code calls it yet; `Spaarke.DocumentOperations/src/hooks/useDocumentActions.ts:66-67,123-128`
        is the precedent (`window.open(desktopUrl)`).
      - **Existing bug**: "View Existing Document" on the duplicate card (`SaveFlow.tsx:1194-1200`) passes a document
        **id** to `onViewDocument`, which expects a URL → a broken link. Fix it with the same record-open.
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-10-03">The layout is the one in the background block. Do not keep the full-screen success card for a successful save. Copy Link keeps copying what it copies today (owner did not ask to change it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-10">Gate on capabilities (`canOpenBrowserWindow`, the existing `canOpenRecord`), never `hostType`. Outlook uses the same shared SaveFlow: after an Outlook save the same form state applies; nothing may become Word-only by branching on host.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent UI v9, semantic tokens, dark mode. Disabled "Saved" must still meet contrast.</constraint>
    <constraint source="security">The collision payload may carry the existing document's id and name ONLY when the existing Read redaction (`OfficeEndpoints.cs:552-597`) passes. Add a SEPARATE boolean (e.g. `canSaveAsVersion`) carrying today's "filed to the target record" rule, and make the client offer "Save as new version" from that flag, not from the id's presence. A caller who cannot Read the other document gets exactly today's payload.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">Open on the collision prompt calls `GET /api/documents/{id}/open-links` (no new route). Use `DesktopUrl` where the host can launch it, else `WebUrl`; decide by capability, not by `hostType`. If the open-links call fails, show its reason inline; never fall back to building a URL client-side.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">`SPAARKE_APP_NAME` is a build setting injected like `ORG_URL`, default `sprk_MatterManagement`; when it is empty, record links are built WITHOUT `appname` (today's behaviour), never with a guessed value. Encode it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF obligations: placement stated (extends `OfficeService`/`OfficeEndpoints`, no new service); publish size measured against a FRESH master build with Compress-Archive, file counts equal on both sides; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` clean.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Client tests in `shared/taskpane/**/__tests__/` and listed in `ci-gated-suites.txt`; server tests in the existing collision contract/unit classes (`OfficeCreateCollisionTests` or the class that owns the 409 payload). No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="parallel wave">Do NOT edit `App.tsx`, `FindView.tsx`, `FindResultsList.tsx`, `useFindRecordMatches.ts` (task 092, running beside you). Do NOT run `npm run build` (the main session runs it after the wave); run jest, lint and typecheck.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">After a successful save (create or version), the form stays: a confirmation bar names the record it was filed to (or says it was saved without a record) with View Document and Copy Link; the footer shows Open Document immediately left of a disabled "Saved" button.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Editing the document name, or a completed Generate Profile, re-enables the button as "Save version", and that save sends `existingDocumentId` = the saved document and `isNewVersion` true. Reverting the name to the saved value returns it to "Saved".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">View Document, Open Document and the duplicate card's "View Existing Document" all open `{ORG_URL}/main.aspx?appname=sprk_MatterManagement&amp;etn=sprk_document&amp;id={id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;navbar=off` (default build setting); with `SPAARKE_APP_NAME` empty, the same URL without `appname`. No path opens the Graph `webUrl` any more.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With `canOpenBrowserWindow` false or `ORG_URL` empty, View Document and Open Document are not rendered (not rendered-and-disabled).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">409 collision, caller CAN Read the other document, it is NOT filed to the target record: the payload carries its id and name and `canSaveAsVersion` false; the prompt shows Keep both, Open and Dismiss — not "Save as new version".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">409 collision, filed to the target record and readable: `canSaveAsVersion` true; the prompt shows Keep both, Save as new version, Open and Dismiss (today's behaviour plus Open).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: 409 collision where the caller CANNOT Read the other document: the payload carries no id, no name and no `canSaveAsVersion` true; the prompt shows Keep both and Dismiss only. A server test pins it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Open calls `GET /api/documents/{id}/open-links` and launches `DesktopUrl` or `WebUrl` per capability; a failed call shows its reason in the prompt.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Gates: gated jest green with new/changed suites listed; lint 0; typecheck 0 production; the BFF Office test scope and ArchTests green; publish delta reported vs fresh master (same tool, equal file counts); CVE check clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Live (after a deploy): a Word save shows the form with "Saved"; View Document opens the record in Matter Management; a collision on a readable, unfiled document offers Open and it opens the file. If no deploy or host is available, leave this open and say so.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>`ms-word:` links cannot be launched from the task pane by any supported call (`window.open`, `Office.context.ui.openBrowserWindow`) — record what was tried and use `WebUrl` everywhere; do not invent a third mechanism.</trigger>
    <trigger>Keeping the form after an Outlook save breaks an Outlook flow the gated suites pin (e.g. saving attachments one after another via "Save Another") — STOP and report the conflict rather than branching on host.</trigger>
    <trigger>The Read redaction cannot be evaluated for the collision's other document without a new Dataverse round trip per 409 that the existing code does not already make — report the cost before adding it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read the files named in the background; trace today's success, collision and Open document record paths end to end, client and server.</step>
    <step>Server: carry the readable existing document's id + name on every collision and add `canSaveAsVersion`; tests for the three cases (readable+filed, readable+unfiled, unreadable).</step>
    <step>Build setting + `appname` in `buildOpenRecordUrl`; tests for both values.</step>
    <step>Client: replace the success card with the saved-form state; Saved / Save version logic; Open Document in the footer; confirmation bar; fix View Existing Document; Open on the collision prompt; tests.</step>
    <step>Gates, publish-size measurement, conflict-check; record in `notes/088-save-tab-after-save.md`; TASK-INDEX 088 → done.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>The saved document id (`useSaveFlow`), the record opener (`openRecordLauncher`), the version-save mode (tasks 023/024), the collision payload and its Read redaction, and `GET /api/documents/{id}/open-links` all exist.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — extends `SaveFlow`'s post-save rendering, `buildOpenRecordUrl` (one parameter), the existing collision payload (one flag) and calls an existing route; no new service, route or component library entry.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>View Document opens Word for the web instead of Spaarke (UAT-1); after a save the user cannot see or re-save the document they are on (UAT-6/7); a collision gives no way to reach the other file (UAT-5); record links open in whatever app the user last used.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Saved form (Word)">
      <steps>
        <step>Save a new document filed to a matter: the form stays, the bar names the matter, the footer reads [Open Document][Saved] with Saved gray.</step>
        <step>Change the name: the button reads "Save version"; save: a new version of the same document, no new row.</step>
        <step>View Document and Open Document open the document record in Matter Management, without the app navigation.</step>
      </steps>
    </test>
    <test name="Collision Open">
      <steps>
        <step>Save a document under the name of an existing, readable document filed elsewhere: the prompt shows Keep both, Open, Dismiss; Open opens that file in Word.</step>
      </steps>
    </test>
    <test name="Outlook unchanged in spirit">
      <steps>
        <step>Save an email in Outlook: the same saved-form state appears; nothing is Word-only.</step>
      </steps>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark mode (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Office dark theme: the bar, the disabled Saved button and the prompt are readable.</step>
      </steps>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

