  <notes>
    Completed 2026-10-03 in wave UAT3-W1 (uncommitted; main session commits). Full record: notes/088-save-tab-after-save.md.
    - Saved state replaces the success card: bar (record / "Not filed to a record.", View Document, Copy Link), name, profile,
      footer [Cancel] [Open Document][Saved]. Name edit or accepted Generate Profile -> "Save version" (FR-11 version of the saved doc).
    - All record links name the app (appname= from SPAARKE_APP_NAME, default sprk_MatterManagement; empty -> none). openRecord
      defaults to the setting, so task 092's Find opens get it too. View Existing Document fixed (id passed as URL).
    - Server: every owned collision carries id + name; new CanSaveAsVersion flag (editable AND filed to target); the Read gate
      strips id, name and flag; flag written only with an id. Pane offers Save as new version from the flag only; Open uses
      GET /api/documents/{id}/open-links.
    - ESCALATION 1 FIRED: ms-word: cannot be launched by a supported call (openBrowserWindow is http/https only, office-js #2820
      by design; window.open of Office URIs undocumented) -> webUrl everywhere, mechanism chosen by canOpenBrowserWindow.
      Trigger 2 not fired (only gated "Save Another" pin was a Word capture test, rewritten, invariant kept). Trigger 3 judged
      not fired: same existing access check, now also on filed-elsewhere collisions (at most 1 OBO access query per refused save).
    - Gates: gated jest 63 suites / 886 tests green (baseline 62/836); lint 0; typecheck 0 production (68 accepted test-file);
      BFF Office scope 467 passed / 8 skipped (pre-existing) / 0 failed; ArchTests 346/346; CVE check clean.
      Publish size OWED (worktree iterated; commit-less branch copy disallowed by the wave rules). Live AC (Word host) OPEN.
    - Owner questions: a version save does not rename (task 023 D-5) though a name edit enables "Save version"; saved state is
      lost on tab remount (App.tsx owns persistence); deploy BFF before the add-in (flag-only version offer).
  </notes>
</task>
